    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Taroki Polish, call king',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Taroki z królami (Taroki call king) is a four-player Polish tarot game from Kozy near Bielsko Biała. Bidder chooses partner by calling a King (not the XIX). 54-card pack, 22 trumps; highest skiż, then XXI down to I, the lowest trump. Objective: bidder's side wins by taking more than half the card points in tricks. Bonuses for all kings, last trick with lowest trump, etc. Card values: skiż/XXI/kings 5, queens 4, cavaliers 3, jacks 2, others 1. From Austrian Tarock tradition in Galicia/Silesia.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'From Kozy near Bielsko-BiaÅ‚a (Poland). Austrian Tarock tradition in Galicia/Silesia; bidder calls a King (not XIX) for partner. 54-card pack, point-trick with bonuses.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four players; temporary partnerships (declarer plus holder of called king vs others, or declarer alone vs three).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card Taroki pack: 22 trumps (skiż, XXI down to I) and four eight-card suits (K, Q, C, J plus four pips).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card Taroki pack, score sheet',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dealer deals 6 cards face down to table (talon), then remaining 48 in batches of 6 so each player receives 12 cards; anticlockwise. Player opposite dealer may refuse to cut; then dealer deals 6 to talon and four packets of 12, and each player in turn chooses a packet.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Higher penalty for giving up with king in talon: Some players set the payment for giving up when the called king is found in the talon at 5 game points rather than 2.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Announced trul score: Some written rules specify 5 game points rather than 4 for announced trul.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
